## Chapter 18: The Core Anomaly
Holding Control Node 4 should have guaranteed an easy two hours of defensive waiting. Anvil Ridge Squad 4 sat firmly at Rank 12 on the public leaderboard, comfortably above the draft line.
While Tobias paced near the shattered glass entrance, keeping his heavy crossbow loaded, and Mina scouted the perimeter alleys, Renna sat on a piece of fallen marble masonry, carefully wiping down her tower shield with an oil rag.
Kaelen leaned against a support pillar in the shadows, his scrap pack resting beside his boots. He kept his eyes half-closed, maintaining his meek, exhausted posture.
Underneath that calm exterior, however, his **[Hive-Mind Synapse]** was working at overdrive.
*Something is wrong with the breach boundary,* Kaelen calculated silently.
The atmospheric pressure inside Sector 4 was dropping rapidly. A subtle, high-frequency tremor—completely distinct from the heavy footsteps of standard monsters—was vibrating through the deep bedrock. It wasn't coming from Sector-C or the commercial ruins of Sector-B.
It was coming directly from **Sector-A Central Core**—where Leon Thorne and Ironclad Academy had been sweeping high-tier beasts for the broadcast drones.
Suddenly, the holographic leaderboard projected above the control node terminal flickered erratically.
*BZZZZT.*
The static cleared, and the live ranking numbers shifted violently in bright crimson light.
**[WARNING: System Node Communications Disrupted in Sector-A!]**
**[Ironclad Squad 1 Status: Signal Lost.]**
**[Gideon Squad 1 Status: Signal Lost.]**
**[System Notice: Sector-A Perimeter Containment Shield Breached!]**
"What?" Tobias froze, pointing his crossbow at the terminal screen. "Signal lost? How does Ironclad lose signal?"
Renna scrambled to her feet, slinging her tower shield over her arm. She ran to the terminal, tapping the diagnostic interface. "The municipal containment grid in the core just went offline. That's impossible—Sector-A is supposed to be fully locked down by the Defense Bureau!"
Above the ruined city, the roaring hum of the corporate broadcast drones suddenly changed pitch. Instead of floating gracefully to capture footage, dozens of silver drones began scattering across the sky, retreating frantically toward the outer staging plaza.
A sharp, panicked voice cut through the emergency radio frequency built into their wrist badges. It was Instructor Horgan’s gravelly voice, distorted by heavy static.
*"—all squads, fall back!—"* Horgan’s voice broke through the speaker. *"—this is not an exercise! A wild Colony Rift has opened inside the Sector-A core! I repeat, a wild Rift! All auxiliary units fall back to the staging gates immediately—!"*
*CRACK-BOOM!*
Before Horgan’s transmission finished, a deafening, thunderous impact rattled the entire five-square-kilometer zone.
Far in the distance, above the high-rise skyline of Sector-A, a massive pillar of dark, obsidian energy shot straight into the sky, tearing open the clouds. The sky above the ruined city turned a sickly, bruised purple as a wave of suffocating, raw monster essence rolled across the sector like a physical gale.
"A wild Rift..." Mina whispered, backing into the atrium, her daggers trembling in her hands. "That means... unrated monsters."
"We're getting out of here," Renna ordered instantly, her voice tight with command. "Tobias, Mina, pack the gear! Kaelen, grab your pack! We head straight for the southern exit gates!"
"Right!" Tobias yelled, grabbing his spare bolts.
Kaelen pulled his scrap pack onto his shoulders, nodding timidly. "Following you, Renna!"
They sprinted out of the glass atrium into the fog-drenched street, heading south toward the safety of the walled staging plaza.
Around them, the fog was no longer white or grey; it was turning a faint, oily purple, heavy with the stench of ozone, copper, and unrefined cosmic essence.
They had only covered two blocks when Mina suddenly skidded to a halt at a major intersection.
"Hold!" she hissed, ducking behind a crushed police vehicle.
Fifty meters ahead, scrambling through the purple haze, were three Ironclad cadets. Their matte-black kinetic plate armor—the expensive gear that was supposed to make them invulnerable—was cracked, scorched, and dripping with dark acid. They had dropped their heavy weapons, sprinting in absolute, blind terror.
Behind them, floating three feet off the ground, was the source of their panic.
It wasn't a standard Colony beast. It was a **Phantasmic Shadow-Stalker**—a creature spawned directly from a raw Cosmic Rift. It looked like a ten-foot panther composed entirely of shifting, void-black smoke, its eyes burning with hollow, crimson flames, its long tail ending in a jagged blade of condensed dark essence.
**[Monster Identification: Phantasmic Shadow-Stalker (Tier-C Elite / Rift Spawn)]**
 * **Attributes:** Intangible Phase-Shift, Essence Corrosion, Blind-Spot Ambush.
 * **Threat Assessment:** Lethal. Physical armor provides negligible protection against dark essence blades.
"Helppp!" one of the fleeing Ironclad cadets shrieked, stumbling over a concrete slab and falling hard onto the asphalt.
The Shadow-Stalker didn't make a sound. It phase-shifted, blurring through the air in a silent, pitch-black streak, appearing directly above the fallen cadet with its dark tail blade raised to impale his neck.
"Tobias! Cover fire!" Renna shouted without thinking, surging forward with her tower shield despite the sheer terror radiating from the beast.
Tobias fired his heavy crossbow. The bolt passed straight through the Shadow-Stalker's smoky flank, dealing zero damage as the beast phased through physical reality.
The creature swiveled its burning crimson eyes away from the Ironclad cadet, locking onto Renna’s approach. It let out a soundless screech that vibrated directly inside everyone's skulls, its smoky tail whipping forward like a black spear.
Renna raised her tower shield, bracing both feet on the ground.
*That essence blade will pass straight through her iron shield,* Kaelen recognized in a microsecond.
His **[Hive-Mind Synapse]** mapped the trajectory of the strike. Renna’s **[Aegis Shield]** class gave her physical defense, but her spiritual resonance was too weak to block a Rift-spawn's phase-attack. If that tail blade hit her shield, it would pass through the metal and sever her shoulder.
The purple fog was thick. The Ironclad cadets were scrambling away with their eyes closed in terror. Tobias and Mina were blinded by the smoke cloud.
*Zero witnesses,* Kaelen calculated.
He didn't pull back. As Renna braced for the impact, Kaelen stepped directly behind her left flank.
He didn't use a flashy spell. He reached out with his bare right index finger, pressing it lightly against the back frame of Renna’s tower shield, right where his **24 Aetheric Resonance** could channel directly into the metal.
"**[Dissect & Assimilate]**—Reverse Flow," Kaelen whispered in the quiet vault of his mind.
He didn't deconstruct the shield. Instead, he forced a micro-pulse of his purified **30 Aetheric Resonance** to surge out through his fingertips into the iron plate, coating the front of Renna's dented shield in a thin, invisible layer of dense, purified essence.
*CLANG-BOOM!*
The Shadow-Stalker’s phase-blade struck the shield—and instead of passing through, it hit Kaelen's invisible resonance layer like a solid steel wall.
The concussive shockwave exploded outward, shattering the asphalt beneath Renna’s boots. The shadow beast let out a real, agonizing shriek as the purified essence burned its dark form, driving the ten-foot monster back ten yards through the air.
Renna blinked, her arms numb from the vibration, staring at her shield in complete, breathless shock. "It... it blocked a Phase-Attack?"
"Renna! Move!" Mina screamed from the alley.
The Shadow-Stalker recovered in mid-air, its crimson eyes burning with demonic rage as it locked onto Kaelen, sensing the true source of the purified energy that had just scorched its form.
It ignored Renna entirely, phasing into a black blur, lunging straight for Kaelen’s throat.
Kaelen lowered his head, let his shoulders slump into a look of absolute panic, and stumbled backward into the deep purple fog of a collapsed side alley, out of sight of his squad.
"Kaelen!" Renna screamed, turning to chase after him.
"Stay back, Renna!" Kaelen’s voice echoed from inside the thick fog, sounding terrified and breathless. "I'll draw it into the narrow alley! Get the Ironclad kids out!"
The moment Kaelen’s boots crossed into the shadow of the collapsed alley, completely hidden from every drone, student, and camera by the thick purple haze, his panicked expression vanished.
His posture straightened instantly. His slouched shoulders squared off.
His dark eyes ignited with a sharp, terrifying coldness as he raised his right hand, his custom concealed bracer gleaming softly beneath his sleeve.
The ten-foot Phantasmic Shadow-Stalker lunged into the narrow alley, its jaws wide, ready to devour the frail Tier-E Salvager.
Kaelen didn't run. He took a single, deliberate step forward, planting his boots with the absolute, unshakable weight of his **[Terrestrial Anchor]**.
"**[Kinetic Overdrive]**," Kaelen growled quietly.
A dark, violent shockwave exploded through his nervous system. His **45 Agility** sped up by 50%, the charging Rift beast dropping into a absolute crawl in his vision.
Kaelen closed his right fist, channeling every drop of his **46 Strength** into a compact, devastating straight punch aimed directly at the center of the shadow beast's burning crimson core.
"Time to see what a Rift monster is made of."
